# Teach the robot a face, or make it forget one.
#
# Enrolment is a deliberate act rather than something that happens
# automatically to everyone the camera sees. Two reasons, and the second is the
# one that actually decides it:
#
#   * Automatically clustering unknown faces fills the gallery with half-seen
#     strangers and mislabels anyone who passes twice.
#   * It would mean the robot builds a biometric record of every person who
#     walks past it, without any of them choosing that. Requiring somebody to
#     ask, by name, keeps the stored set to people who opted in.
#
#   ros2 service call /face_identity/enroll burgerbot_msgs/srv/EnrollPerson \
#       "{name: mark}"
#
# The call blocks while it captures several views, so stand in front of the
# camera and turn your head slowly until it returns.

string name

# Delete this person instead of enrolling them. The gallery is the only copy;
# once saved over, the embeddings are gone.
bool forget false

---

bool success
string message

# How many stored views this person now has.
uint32 views
